            <ArticleTitle>Large, isolated, congenital aneurysm of the anterior descending coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>274-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A large congenital aneurysm, arising from the first diagonal branch of the left anterior descending artery in a 52 year old woman was diagnosed by transoesophageal echocardiography, computed tomography, and magnetic resonance imaging. Surgical closure of the aneurysm was successful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
